        "subject": "LU-20732 ptlrpc: fix nodemap_del() deadlock",
        "message": "LU-20732 ptlrpc: fix nodemap_del() deadlock\n\nThis patch is used to fix nodemap_del() deadlock.\n\nThe nodemap_del() function removes the nodemap procfs entry\nwhile it still holds active_config_lock.\nRemoving a procfs entry will wait for the processes already\nhold it open, so the caller may block with the lock held.\nMean time the config log thread may run the upcall\n\"/usr/sbin/lctl set_param nodemap.<name>.fileset=...\"\nand wait for it to finish.\nThat lctl cmd opens the same procfs entry.\nThe entry's write handler needs active_config_lock,\nwhich was already held by nodemap_del() function.\nThe two sides waits for the other,\ncauses sanity-sec test_27ac hangs and time out.\n\nRemoves the entry after the lock is dropped.\nnm_pde_data is cleared under the lock,\nso no other thread can pick the entry up while it is going away.\nThis is the order nodemap_destroy() already uses.\n\nBecause the old entry may still exist for a second after the lock\nis dropped, lprocfs_nodemap_register() now returns -EEXIST instead of\ngoing on with a NULL proc entry.\nSo let nodemap_add() rolls back and retries a few times.\n\nFixes: c6e12f54dc95 (\"LU-18357 ptlrpc: Fix fileset llog compatibility on nodemaps\")\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=27ac\nSigned-off-by: Xiyang Wang <xiwang@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I552ed69ee22663bc1c635d43cca5cd8af75e3c88\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
